wayfarmap.option.minimap.showCoordinates=Coordinates
wayfarmap.option.minimap.showCoordinates.desc=Show your coordinates under the minimap.
wayfarmap.option.minimap.showBiome=Biome
wayfarmap.option.minimap.showBiome.desc=Show the current biome under the minimap.
wayfarmap.option.minimap.textScale=Text size
wayfarmap.option.minimap.textScale.desc=Size of the coordinates and the biome under the minimap: 1.00 is the game's font, smaller or bigger from 0.50 to 2.00.
wayfarmap.option.minimap.textGap=Room from the map
wayfarmap.option.minimap.textGap.desc=Room between the minimap and the coordinates and biome under it, in pixels.
wayfarmap.option.map.lightMode=Lighting
wayfarmap.option.map.lightMode.desc=Auto follows the day/night cycle; Day and Night fix the look of the map.
wayfarmap.option.map.lightMode.auto=Auto
wayfarmap.option.map.lightMode.day=Day
wayfarmap.option.map.lightMode.night=Night
wayfarmap.option.map.useTextureColors=Texture colors
wayfarmap.option.map.useTextureColors.desc=Color blocks by their texture (supports resource packs and mods). Off: vanilla map colors. Applies as chunks are rescanned.
wayfarmap.option.map.seeThroughGlass=See through glass
wayfarmap.option.map.seeThroughGlass.desc=Show what is under glass, lightly tinted with its color. Applies as chunks are rescanned.
wayfarmap.option.map.biomeColorSaturation=Biome color saturation
wayfarmap.option.map.biomeColorSaturation.desc=Saturation and contrast of grass, leaves and water colors on the 2D map (1.0 = the game's own, lower is more muted, higher more vivid). Transitions between biomes stay smooth. Applies as chunks are rescanned.
wayfarmap.option.map.isoPlayerModel=Player as a 3D model
wayfarmap.option.map.isoPlayerModel.desc=On the 3D map, show yourself as your 3D model (skin, armor, walking, where you look) instead of the arrow.
wayfarmap.option.map.showPlants=Grass and flowers
wayfarmap.option.map.showPlants.desc=Draw grass and flowers on the 2D map. Off: the block under them is shown (the "2D map without plants" mode). Areas mapped before this mode existed keep them until mapped again.
wayfarmap.option.map.chunksScannedPerTick=Chunks per tick
wayfarmap.option.map.chunksScannedPerTick.desc=How many loaded chunks are drawn into the map per tick. Lower if the game stutters.
wayfarmap.option.map.autosaveIntervalSeconds=Autosave (s)
wayfarmap.option.map.autosaveIntervalSeconds.desc=How often the explored map is saved to disk.
wayfarmap.option.entities.showOtherPlayers=Players
wayfarmap.option.entities.showOtherPlayers.desc=Show other players with their face.
wayfarmap.option.entities.showHostileMobs=Hostile mobs
wayfarmap.option.entities.showHostileMobs.desc=Show monsters (red frame).
wayfarmap.option.entities.showPassiveMobs=Neutral mobs
wayfarmap.option.entities.showPassiveMobs.desc=Show cows, sheep and other animals (grey frame).
wayfarmap.option.entities.showAmbientMobs=Ambient mobs
wayfarmap.option.entities.showAmbientMobs.desc=Show bats and other ambient creatures (purple frame).
wayfarmap.option.entities.showOtherEntities=Friendly mobs
wayfarmap.option.entities.showOtherEntities.desc=Show villagers, traders (like hobgoblins), golems and other NPCs (green frame).
wayfarmap.option.entities.icons=Mob icons
wayfarmap.option.entities.icons.desc=Draw mobs as a small icon of their face. Off: colored dots.
wayfarmap.option.entities.iconLimit=Icon limit
wayfarmap.option.entities.iconLimit.desc=Only the nearest mobs get an icon, the rest are dots.
wayfarmap.option.entities.verticalRange=Height range
wayfarmap.option.entities.verticalRange.desc=Only show mobs at most this many blocks above or below you. Mobs below you fade out the lower they are, and are gone at this distance.
wayfarmap.option.entities.showPets=Pets
wayfarmap.option.entities.showPets.desc=Show tamed mobs: wolves, cats, horses, modded pets (blue frame).
wayfarmap.option.entities.frameWidth=Frame width
wayfarmap.option.entities.frameWidth.desc=Width of the colored frame around mob icons that tells what kind of mob it is, in pixels. 0 turns the frame off.
wayfarmap.option.entities.frameOpacity=Frame opacity, %%
wayfarmap.option.entities.frameOpacity.desc=How opaque the colored frame around mob icons is: lower lets the map show through it.
wayfarmap.option.entities.iconScale=Icon size, %%
wayfarmap.option.entities.iconScale.desc=Size of mob icons on both maps, in percent of the usual size.
wayfarmap.option.entities.facing=Where mobs look
wayfarmap.option.entities.facing.desc=A small arrow at each mob's icon pointing where it looks.
wayfarmap.option.entities.hostileNames=Hostile mob names
wayfarmap.option.entities.hostileNames.desc=Show the names of hostile mobs given with a name tag under their icon.
wayfarmap.option.entities.neutralNames=Neutral mob names
wayfarmap.option.entities.neutralNames.desc=Show the names of neutral mobs (animals and the like) given with a name tag under their icon.
wayfarmap.option.entities.ambientNames=Ambient mob names
wayfarmap.option.entities.ambientNames.desc=Show the names of ambient mobs (bats and the like) given with a name tag under their icon.
wayfarmap.option.entities.friendlyNames=Friendly mob names
wayfarmap.option.entities.friendlyNames.desc=Show the names of friendly mobs (villagers, golems) given with a name tag under their icon.
wayfarmap.option.entities.petNames=Pet names
wayfarmap.option.entities.petNames.desc=Show the names of pets (given with a name tag) under their icon.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.showInWorld=In world
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.showInWorld.desc=Show waypoint markers in the world.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.showOnMinimap=On minimap
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.showOnMinimap.desc=Show waypoints on the minimap.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.minimapSize=Marker size on minimap
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.minimapSize.desc=Size of waypoint markers on the minimap, in pixels: 8 is the usual size.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.scale=Size in world
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.scale.desc=Overall size of in-world waypoints.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.minScale=Minimum size
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.minScale.desc=Waypoints shrink with distance down to this fraction of their close-up size, then stop.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.maxDistance=View distance
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.maxDistance.desc=Farther waypoints are not shown in the world. 0 = no limit.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.labelMaxWidth=Name width
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.labelMaxWidth.desc=Longer names are cut with '...'. Hover a waypoint on the map to see its full name.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.mapLabels=Names on the world map
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.mapLabels.desc=Waypoint names on the world map (2D and 3D): always, or only for the waypoint under the mouse.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.mapLabels.always=Always
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.mapLabels.hover=On hover
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.worldLabels=Names in the world
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.worldLabels.desc=Waypoint names in the world (with the distance): always, or only for the waypoint you look at; before, its icon alone.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.worldLabels.always=Always
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.worldLabels.look=When looked at
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.lookZone=Look zone, degrees
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.lookZone.desc=With names shown when looked at: how far off the waypoint's icon the crosshair may be for the name to show, in degrees. 0: only on the icon.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.fadeNear=Fade when near
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.fadeNear.desc=In-world waypoints (marker and beam) fade out smoothly as you come near them.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.fadeStart=Start fading at, blocks
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.fadeStart.desc=In-world waypoints start fading this many blocks away.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.fadeEnd=Gone at, blocks
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.fadeEnd.desc=In-world waypoints are gone this many blocks away (closer than where they start fading).
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.deathPoints=Death marker
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.deathPoints.desc=Place a waypoint where you die.
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.deathPointsKeep=Keep
wayfarmap.option.waypoints.deathPointsKeep.desc=How many death markers to keep; older ones are removed.
